::: table | The Topic 1 one-liner bank.
@widths 7.5,6.5
@font 9.5
Question | Answer
Who first distinguished sex from gender identity in psychology? | Robert Stoller, *Sex and Gender* (1968)
Who brought the sex/gender distinction into sociology? | Ann Oakley, *Sex, Gender and Society* (1972)
Who coined the term "gender role"? | John Money (1955)
"One is not born, but rather becomes, a woman" — who, and where? | Simone de Beauvoir, *The Second Sex* (1949)
Beauvoir's term for woman as defined by man | "The Other"
Where was one of the first Women's Studies courses taught? | Cornell University (1969)
The first Women's Studies programme | San Diego State College (1970)
US National Women's Studies Association founded | 1977
Editors who framed the autonomy/integration debate | Gloria Bowles and Renate Duelli Klein, *Theories of Women's Studies* (1983)
Autonomy means … | A separate Women's/Gender Studies department with its own staff and degrees
Integration means … | Weaving gender into every existing discipline (mainstreaming)
The resolution of the debate | The dual strategy — an autonomous base that drives integration
The main risk of autonomy | Ghettoisation
The main risk of integration | Dilution ("add women and stir")
India's 1974 report on women's status | *Towards Equality*
Year Women's Studies centres were set up in five Pakistani universities | 1989
The five universities of 1989 | Quaid-i-Azam (Islamabad), Karachi, Punjab (Lahore), Peshawar, Balochistan (Quetta)
Which university houses a Centre of Excellence in Gender Studies (MCQ 2016)? | Quaid-i-Azam University
A Pakistani academic journal of gender studies (MCQ 2018) | *Pakistan Journal of Gender Studies*
Gender Studies entered the CSS optional scheme in | CE-2016 (Group V, code 31)
"Gender … is a primary way of signifying relationships of power" | Joan Wallach Scott (1986)
Author of *If Women Counted* (unpaid work and GDP) | Marilyn Waring (1988)
Author of *In a Different Voice* (ethic of care) | Carol Gilligan (1982)
Author of *The Creation of Patriarchy* | Gerda Lerner (1986)
Author of *The Sexual Contract* | Carole Pateman (1988)
Who argued sexual harassment is sex discrimination? | Catharine MacKinnon (1979)
Who coined "the male gaze"? | Laura Mulvey (1975)
*Sex and Temperament in Three Primitive Societies* | Margaret Mead (1935) — Arapesh, Mundugumor, Tchambuli
"What is now called the nature of women is an eminently artificial thing" | John Stuart Mill, *The Subjection of Women* (1869)
*The Social Construction of Reality* | Peter Berger and Thomas Luckmann (1966)
The "sex/gender system" | Gayle Rubin, "The Traffic in Women" (1975)
*The History of Sexuality*, vol. 1 — power produces discourse on sexuality | Michel Foucault (1976)
"Doing Gender" | Candace West and Don Zimmerman (1987)
Gender is "performative" | Judith Butler, *Gender Trouble* (1990)
Gender as a social institution | Judith Lorber, *Paradoxes of Gender* (1994)
Gender as a social structure | Barbara Risman (2004)
Social learning theory of gender | Albert Bandura; Walter Mischel (1966)
Stages of gender identity, stability, constancy | Lawrence Kohlberg (1966)
Gender schema theory | Sandra Bem (1981)
Androgyny and the Bem Sex-Role Inventory | Sandra Bem (1974)
An androgynous person has … | Both (positive) masculine and feminine traits
Who coined "queer theory"? | Teresa de Lauretis (1990–91)
*Epistemology of the Closet* | Eve Kosofsky Sedgwick (1990)
The "one-sex" model of the body | Thomas Laqueur, *Making Sex* (1990)
"The Five Sexes" | Anne Fausto-Sterling (1993)
The assumption that heterosexuality is the only norm | Heteronormativity
Intersex in classical Islamic law | *Khuntha*
Who coined "hegemonic masculinity"? | R. W. (Raewyn) Connell
Connell's four masculinities | Hegemonic, complicit, marginalised, subordinated
Men's collective gain from women's subordination (Connell) | The patriarchal dividend
Connell's term for femininity that accommodates men | Emphasised femininity
"Is Female to Male as Nature Is to Culture?" | Sherry Ortner (1974)
The plough and gender roles | Ester Boserup (1970); Alesina, Giuliano and Nunn (2013)
The theory that evolution and androgens explain universal male crime | Evolutionary neuroandrogenic theory (Lee Ellis)
*Delusions of Gender* | Cordelia Fine (2010)
The "mosaic" brain | Daphna Joel (2015)
The John/Joan case | David Reimer (raised as a girl after a 1966 accident; reverted to male)
*Language and Woman's Place* | Robin Lakoff (1975)
*Man Made Language* | Dale Spender (1980)
"Rapport talk" and "report talk" | Deborah Tannen (1990)
Semantic derogation of women's words | Muriel Schulz (1975)
Deconstruction and binary oppositions | Jacques Derrida (1967)
Hatred of women | Misogyny
A hierarchical system dominated by men | Patriarchy
Supreme Court recognition of a third gender on CNICs | 2009 (Dr Muhammad Aslam Khaki case)
Colonial law that labelled "eunuchs" a criminal class | Criminal Tribes Act 1871
Transgender persons counted in the 2017 Census | 10,418
Transgender Persons (Protection of Rights) Act | 2018
Federal Shariat Court judgment on the Transgender Act | 19 May 2023 (ss. 2(f), 3, 7 held repugnant; appeal pending)
:::
